  "slug": "paul-pierce-lost-100k-and-woke-up-with-12-voicemail-from-espns-hr-department",
  "postId": 73941,
  "title": "Paul Pierce lost $100K And Woke Up With 12 Voicemails From ESPN's HR Department",
  "htmlContent": "<!-- wp:image {\"id\":510994,\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img class=\"wp-image-510994\" src=\"http://landonbuford.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/04/GettyImages-141031235-678x1024.jpg\" alt=\"\" />\n<figcaption>BOSTON, MA - MARCH 09: Paul Pierce #34 of the Boston Celtics celebrates a three point shot in the second half against the Portland Trail Blazers on March 9, 2012 at TD Garden in Boston, Massachusetts. The Boston Celtics defeated the Portland Trail Blazers 104-86. NOTE TO USER: User expressly acknowledges and agrees that, by downloading and or using this photograph, User is consenting to the terms and conditions of the Getty Images License Agreement. (Photo by Elsa/Getty Images)</figcaption>\n</figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>On Friday night, 2021 Hall of Fame Finalist Paul Pierce made headlines for going on Instagram Live. The former 10-time All-Star was featured smoking, playing poker, and a room full of strippers.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:embed {\"url\":\"https://twitter.com/barstoolsports/status/1378327835228659712?s=20\",\"type\":\"rich\",\"providerNameSlug\":\"twitter\",\"responsive\":true,\"className\":\"\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-rich is-provider-twitter wp-block-embed-twitter\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\">https://twitter.com/barstoolsports/status/1378327835228659712?s=20</div>\n</figure>\n<!-- /wp:embed -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>According to Twitter user, @big_business_ shared the Paul Pierce \"was requesting an escort to 315 viewers on IG Live; I fuck with the vision even though he’s about to be in the ESPN gulag.\"</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:embed {\"url\":\"https://twitter.com/big_business_/status/1378243273077186560?s=20\",\"type\":\"rich\",\"providerNameSlug\":\"twitter\",\"responsive\":true,\"className\":\"\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-rich is-provider-twitter wp-block-embed-twitter\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\">https://twitter.com/big_business_/status/1378243273077186560?s=20</div>\n</figure>\n<!-- /wp:embed -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><a href=\"https://twitter.com/jtylerconway/status/1378330250975776768?s=20\">Per Bleacher Report's Tyler Conway</a>, \"Paul Pierce woke up, down $100k and with 12 voicemails from ESPN Human Resources.\"</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>It didn't take long for NBA fans and the rest of Twitter to ask what ESPN and Disney thought about Pierce's actions.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Pierce has been an ESPN NBA analyst for the network’s NBA coverage on <em>NBA Countdown</em> and <em>The Jump</em>. He joined ESPN as a regular studio analyst in August ahead of the 2017-18 NBA season. Previously, he joined ESPN’s and ABC’s <em>NBA Countdown</em> as a guest analyst during the 2017 and 2016 NBA Finals. </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Earlier tonight, Pierce tweeted \"Good Morning\" make many people believe that he was just waking up from his hibernation.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:embed {\"url\":\"https://twitter.com/paulpierce34/status/1378540504627830787?s=20\",\"type\":\"rich\",\"providerNameSlug\":\"twitter\",\"responsive\":true,\"className\":\"\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-rich is-provider-twitter wp-block-embed-twitter\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\">https://twitter.com/paulpierce34/status/1378540504627830787?s=20</div>\n</figure>\n<!-- /wp:embed -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>During his career, Pierce won a championship in 2008 and was named Fi nals MVP.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->",
